          "type": "turn",
          "question": "When a code must never be sequenced first, how is that shown in the classification?",
          "answer": "In ICD-10-CM, when an underlying condition must be reported before its manifestation, this sequencing is shown with the pair of instructions: \"Code first\" and \"use additional code.\" This indicates that the code for the underlying condition should be sequenced first, and the code for the manifestation should follow it. This information comes from the document \"ICD-10-CM code structure and the conventions that govern selection.\"\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
